{
  "requirement": "After one valid judgment, the harness MUST write the subject text, submitted\ndetermination and rationale, and recorded inputs using the existing evidence\nschema. {cite}`requirements.ci.schema`\nBy default, it MUST write the subject's evidence file. With `--stdout`, it MUST\nemit a single evidence JSON object followed by a newline to stdout and MUST NOT\ncreate or change evidence files or directories. All three outcomes MUST be\nwritten to the selected destination as completed assessments; their validation\nstatus MUST follow {cite}`requirements.ci.determination`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "## Judgment: the persistence requirement is met\n\n### What the requirement asks for\nAfter one valid judgment, the harness must:\n- write the subject text, determination, rationale and recorded inputs in the existing evidence schema;\n- write the subject's evidence file by default;\n- with `--stdout`, emit a single evidence JSON object plus a newline and create or change no evidence files or directories;\n- write all three outcomes (true, false, FIXME) as completed assessments;\n- leave validation status to `requirements.ci.determination`.\n\n### Implementation\n- **Record construction.** `assess` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` builds the record after the single accepted `submit_judgment`:\n  - It has the form `{<requirement|example>: subject_text, determination, rationale, references, inputs}`.\n  - That matches the `requirements.ci.schema` shape (the schema's own text carries that definition).\n  - `Judgment::to_value` in `src/judgment.rs` serialises `true`, `false` and `{\"FIXME\": [...]}`.\n  - Multiple or invalid submissions return an error before any record exists, so only valid judgments are persisted.\n- **Single-subject path.** `configured_assessment` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` pretty-prints the record plus `\\n`.\n  - By default it creates `evidence/` and writes `evidence/<subject>.json`.\n  - With `EvidenceOutput::Stdout` it writes only that JSON to stdout, flushes, and creates no evidence path. Usage state lives outside the project; `usage_state_root` rejects an in-project location.\n  - Only after the write succeeds does it set `evidence_written` and report the outcome.\n  - Clap makes `--all` conflict with `--stdout`, so stdout mode is always single-subject.\n- **Batch path.** `write_record` in `src/authoring/batch.rs` writes the same record to `evidence/<name>.json` through a temp file and atomic persist. `PendingAssessment::persisted` then marks the assessment completed.\n- **No extra behaviour and no unmarked implementation.** All three outcomes follow the same path. Validation status comes from `requirements.ci.determination` (false fails, true and FIXME pass), and the persistence code does not intercept it. The `{cite}` on `PendingAssessment` is a plain data holder for the pending record, so it does not leave part of the requirement unmarked.\n\n### Test coverage\n- **Stdout.** `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` covers true, false and FIXME, with and without `--verbose`.\n  - It parses the whole stdout as a single JSON value ending in a newline.\n  - It checks the subject text, determination, rationale and inputs.\n  - It checks that the existing evidence file is byte-identical, and that the `evidence/` directory is not created when it was absent.\n  - It checks that the usage record is `completed` with `evidence_output: stdout`.\n- **File output.** `false_is_a_completed_assessment` and `verbose_single_author_reports_only_false_rationale_without_source_inputs` cover false and true.\n  - They check the file contents and the completed usage record.\n  - `false_is_a_completed_assessment` also checks that outline inputs hold selectors and hashes rather than source text.\n  - It also checks that `validate_repository` rejects the false record with its rationale.\n- **Batch.** `terminal_progress_distinguishes_judgments_from_authoring_errors` writes true, false and FIXME records, and two batch tests check that denied reads leave other assessments' evidence intact:\n  - `denied_read_aborts_only_its_assessment_and_runs_queued_assessments`\n  - `denied_read_preserves_in_flight_assessments_and_their_evidence`\n  - `batch_fills_evidence_preserves_current_records_and_reauthors_only_changed_inputs` in `tests/authoring_batch.rs` also asserts that the written true and FIXME records pass `validate_repository` with no errors.\n  - The reference-set batch test checks that the `references` digest is written.\n- **Failure paths.**\n  - `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage` makes the write fail and checks that `evidence_written` is false and the usage outcome is `failed` while the accepted judgment is still recorded.\n  - `explicit_untracked_reads_abort_without_another_request_or_evidence_write` checks that an aborted assessment leaves the existing evidence untouched and `evidence_written` false.\n- **Live provider.** `live_bedrock_authoring` checks stdout mode against a real provider, and `Server::start_with` and `Fixture::new` are the shared test infrastructure.\n\n### Minor observation\nNo single test asserts the `references` field on the single-subject file or stdout output. Batch tests check it and `assess` builds it uniformly, so I don't count this as a gap.\n\nNo FIXME or other acknowledged gaps are present or needed.",
  "references": "9c3222b86009f0ddc45d3d47d37c33b1547175f1c410c942f1a9cccf5521ac4b",
